The desk merged 412 unique reports into #4471. The export contains 427 rows because its pages
overlap: 15 report IDs appear twice. Grouping the unique reports by tenant locale and booking
form, rather than intake tag or subject, reveals two problems.

<Incident4471Summary />

## Parser: 379 reports

The shared parser reads dates month first for day-first tenants. Bookings and calendar invites
can land on a different date. This is the majority cause assigned to #4471. It spans app,
email, and form reports across 11 tenants. Fix the parser and verify day-first locales with
dates whose day and month can both be read as a month.

## Form hint: 33 reports

Booking-v3 shows `MM/DD/YYYY` to people whose tenant uses a day-first locale. A person entering
the date shown by the hint can have it read in their tenant's order. These are form reports
from Alder Physio, Copper Studio, and Pale Harbour. Correct the hint and verify form entry
separately from the parser fix.

## Triage

The accepted subject-only duplicate rule merged distinct causes into #4471. Intake tags also
disagree with the cause for some reports. Classify by tenant locale, booking form, and channel;
deduplicate by report ID before counting. The five reports in `desk-notes.json` that were read
as one-day moves stay under their tenant-derived cause.

The desk is still working. Recheck the live ticket and newer reports before treating these
export counts as current.

